  form: theorem
  span:
    file: PrimesCongruentOne.lean
    lines: 68-70
  digest: aa7e6cbd249c3ce0
  says: For every natural number k, if k is not 0, then the set of natural numbers p such that p is prime and p
    is congruent to 1 modulo k is infinite.
  quantifiers:
  - kind: for-all
    what: natural numbers k with k not 0
  - kind: infinitely-many
    what: natural numbers p that are prime and congruent to 1 modulo k
  reached: 'yes'
