- id: C:step/order-is-k
  type: step
  name: The order of b modulo p is k
  summary: Since b is nonzero modulo p, its multiplicative order divides p - 1.
  stance: opinion
  inside: C:lemma/Nat.exists_prime_gt_modEq_one
  says: Since b is nonzero modulo p, its multiplicative order divides p - 1. Since k divides b and p does not, k
    is nonzero modulo p, so a root of the k-th cyclotomic polynomial there is a primitive k-th root of unity and
    the order of b is exactly k. Hence k divides p - 1, that is, p is congruent to 1 modulo k.
  span:
    file: PrimesCongruentOne.lean
    lines: 53-59
  confidence: high
  provenance:
    mode: derived
