- id: N:decision/evaluate-at-k-times-n-factorial
  type: decision
  name: Evaluate at k times n factorial
  summary: The point b where the cyclotomic polynomial is evaluated is k times n factorial.
  stance: opinion
  chose: b = k times n factorial
  because: The factor k keeps k nonzero modulo p, the factor n factorial keeps p above n, and b is at least 2 so
    the value exceeds 1; a smaller multiple such as k times the least common multiple of 1 to n would also serve.
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - PrimesCongruentOne.lean
    confidence: 0.35
    state: known
  made:
